    "id": "MA102",
    "sec": "technical",
    "topic": "Engineering Mathematics",
    "diff": "Medium",
    "q": "Evaluate the contour integral ∮_C [1 / (z - 3)] dz around the circle C: |z| = 5 oriented counter-clockwise.",
    "opts": [
      "0",
      "2 π i",
      "π i",
      "4 π i"
    ],
    "ans": 1,
    "sol": "The simple pole at z = 3 lies strictly inside the contour |z| = 5. By Cauchy's Integral Formula, ∮_C [f(z) / (z - z₀)] dz = 2πi f(z₀) = 2πi(1) = 2πi.",
    "form": "Cauchy Integral Formula: ∮ 1/(z - a) dz = 2πi.",
