    "ans": 3,
    "sol": "Let total marks be M. Pass marks = 40% of M. Candidate got 32% of M and fell short by 24. So, 40% of M - 32% of M = 24 marks => (40 - 32)% of M = 24 => 8% of M = 24. M = (24 × 100) / 8 = 300 marks.",
    "form": "Maximum Marks = (Failing Margin × 100) / (% Pass - % Scored)",
    "exam": "Placement"
