    "topic": "Mixtures and Alligations",
    "diff": "Easy",
    "q": "In what ratio must a grocer mix two varieties of pulses costing ₹15/kg and ₹20/kg respectively so that the resulting mixture is worth ₹18/kg?",
    "opts": [
      "3 : 3",
      "3 : 2",
      "2 : 3",
      "2 : 4"
    ],
    "ans": 2,
    "sol": "By the Rule of Alligation: (Cheaper Quantity) / (Dearer Quantity) = (Price of Dearer - Mean Price) / (Mean Price - Price of Cheaper) = (20 - 18) / (18 - 15) = 2 / 3. Reducing to lowest terms gives 2 : 3.",
    "form": "Q_cheaper : Q_dearer = (P_dearer - P_mean) : (P_mean - P_cheaper)",
    "exam": "Placement"
