    "ans": 2,
    "sol": "By the Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion for two sets: n(A ∪ B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A ∩ B) = 65 + 55 - 30 = 90. The number of residents reading neither newspaper is the complement: n((A ∪ B)') = Total - n(A ∪ B) = 100 - 90 = 10.",
    "form": "n(A ∪ B)' = Total - [n(A) + n(B) - n(A ∩ B)]",
    "exam": "Placement"
